      "text": "The graph of a function has an $x$-line which goes through the origin and $y$-axis when the domain covers the entire real numbers.\n\nThe graphs are shown below:\n\n\nGraph A shows $x$ as starting at a positive infinite point and ending at a negative finite point.\n\nGraph B is simply one point mapping to multiple points.\n\nGraph C is $x$ coming from the negatives to the positive infinite point and $y$ increasing to an infintely large value.\n\nGraph D is negative $x$ mapping onto a negative $y$ and negative $x$ mapping onto a positive $y$. The inverse is drawn diagnostically by switching the coordinates of the points.\n\nGraph E has one point mapping to multiple points.\n\n$\\boxed{\\text{C}}$",
